NAME
       ioport_read, ioport_write - access an I/O port

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int      cervus_ioport_write(uint16_t port, uint8_t width, uint32_t val);
       uint32_t cervus_ioport_read(uint16_t port, uint8_t width);

DESCRIPTION
       Reads and writes an x86 I/O port from user space, with a width
       of 1, 2 or 4 bytes. Reserved for driver bring-up and hardware
       poking from a program instead of from the kernel.

       There is no arbitration: writing to a port a driver owns will
       confuse it. Requires the capability, so an ordinary user cannot
       reach the hardware this way.

RETURN VALUE
       The value read, or negative on failure.

ERRORS
       EPERM   the caller lacks the capability

SEE ALSO
       pci_list(2), cap(2), lspci(1)
